<!--Post: 8471--><!--Time: 1109166269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8471"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 5:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I guess I have been reading here waaayyy too much as I am starting to have dreams about this freak. <BR> <BR>I dreamt last night that he was caught.  He was 40ish, had long hair, an Army fatigue jacket, jeans, and glasses.  He seemed pretty calm also.   <BR> <BR>Has anyone else had dreams?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8471-->
<!--Post: 8510--><!--Time: 1109180387-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8510"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m visiting my mother and when I&#39;m about to enter the rear door to the kitchen I notice the door is open. I look inside and see my mom plopped on a chair with blood all over her shirt. She looked dead. <BR> <BR>Terrified, I run to the next room to use the phone to summon help, but when I reach the phone its line was cut.  <BR> <BR>When I turn around to get out of the house, I see my mom standing right in front of me. She looks at me and says, &#34;I&#39;m not dead, see? It was only one shot!&#34;... then she laughs with a satanic voice. <BR> <BR>Then, all of a sudden I hear a gun blast, and see my mom drop dead, and I see BTK behind her. <BR> <BR>BTK is an old, short, wrinkly woman with a huge hump on her back. She says &#34;how are uuuuuuuu?&#34; while aiming her gun at me and giving me a demonic look... then I know I&#39;m in trouble. <BR> <BR>I run back to the kitchen to get out of the house, but she cuts me off and shoots me... <BR> <BR>LMAO! No, I do not hate my mommie. <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8510-->
<!--Post: 8598--><!--Time: 1109224038-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8598"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 9:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I haven&#39;t had any dreams the last few weeks about him, but these are the two I had in early February: <BR> <BR>One night I dreamt that I saw 4 shadowy towers with large birds flying up towards them as if I was seeing through his eyes. The sky was very overcast. I didn&#39;t know what this meant &#40;if anything&#41;, but I did take the time to look up &#34;four towers and Wichita&#34;. I came up with the new bridges at West Douglas and Lewis Streets. I had no idea they existed until then as I don&#39;t live in the state of Kansas and I&#39;ve never been there in my life! So I&#39;m wondering if he actually lives close to the river &#40;maybe the other side&#41; or if he walks on the riverwalk or the nearby park sometimes. <BR> <BR>Then a few nights later on, I dreamt that he was asking a female victim, &#34;Do you go to church?&#34; I hear her saying, &#34;Yes.&#34; He replies, &#34;Good. Then you know where you&#39;re going after I&#39;m done with you.&#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8598-->
<!--Post: 10226--><!--Time: 1109828188-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10226"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 9:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I had a dream about him the night he was arrested. It was horrible. He was in custody, but would viciously attack people, including me. A doctor was escorting him around and had a syringe on a pole and would zap him to calm him down. The meds did not last long enough. People were looking for clues. I asked the police why he was not shackled, both hands and feet. They told me that they could not afford to buy shackles. I told them that I would be glad to foot the bill. It was impossible to control him. He was not even cuffed! <BR> <BR>He looks PO&#39;d in his jailhouse pics on the news.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10226-->
<!--Post: 10230--><!--Time: 1109829501-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10230"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 9:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I will risk sounding truly weird, but I didn&#39;t actually have a dream about BTK. I had something stranger - a daydream. <BR> <BR>It seems like I&#39;d been up all night, and was posting on one of the boards. I think ks.com. <BR> <BR>It was a few weeks after I&#39;d done my profile of him - maybe longer, January, actually - and the sun was up and everything was quiet. I was very tired. If you stay up late once too often, the supernatural world of your subconscious will start to push it&#39;s fingertips through the fabric between the worlds and invade your waking reality a bit.  <BR> <BR>It wasn&#39;t a hallucination; much more like a malignant daydream. As I sat here, reading and posting - it was also the night I first found the EAR/ONS page - <a href="http://www.ear-ons.com" target=_top>http://www.ear-ons.com</a> - I had a movie run through my head.  <BR> <BR><i>I stood from my leather desk chair and checked on my sleeping children. I switched off the computer, and decided I wanted a little light in the room while I rested - I worked night shift for years, and actually can find light while I&#39;m sleeping a sort of comfort. I raised the blinds in our bedroom here that look out onto the carport. And there he was. As I&#39;d described him before, stocky, balding, with a mustache, wearing slightly over-large glasses. Staring. A steady, unblinking, frozen, malevolent stare.</i> <BR> <BR>I said to myself, &#34;time to back away from the effing computer and re-join the real world.&#34; <BR> <BR>And I did. <BR> <BR>Now that I know what his face truly looks like, that nightmare vision, for me, has changed very little.  <BR> <BR>I always keep that shade closed, now. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10230-->
<!--Post: 10258--><!--Time: 1109859553-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10258"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 6:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You may have actually summoned part of him in that revelation. I believe in the seen and unseen, and I am never surprised at what the human mind and spirit can accomplish. Or you teleported in some way to connect with him. The final frontier: the human spirit. Don&#39;t be surprised to find that one of your children has a special gift in that area.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10258-->
<!--Post: 10505--><!--Time: 1109976359-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10505"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 2:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;...Don&#39;t be surprised to find that one of your children has a special gift in that area...&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>I wish you hadn&#39;t said that. I&#39;ll not go into it, but if there are such things as you say, then it&#39;s likely that 2 of my four children definitely DO have it. Both are, like me, redheads. I don&#39;t know why I find that significant, but it is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10505-->
<!--Post: 10568--><!--Time: 1110008789-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10568"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 11:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I ate half a batch of brownies before sleeping and had a continuous dream that I woke from and re-entered several times that was kind of a cross of Salvidore Dali meets Dr Seuss. It revolved around Wichita, particularly WSU and played out in surprising details some of the scenarios found on this web site.  <BR> <BR>Denny never showed and it was more of a cartoon than a nightmare. I don&#39;t know...Denny , to me, looks too much like George on Seinfeld for me to really work up a good terror.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10568-->
